<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Make Honey EVEN MORE Compatible (TSP.zal.patchhoney2, Workshop 2959585309, Zaljerem, Steaplay, TurtleShroom).

  That mod already supports the megabee by defName (its root Patches/TSP_MegaBee_CanIntoHoney.xml, read
  2026-10-09): MegabeeTallow joins a "Mega Bees" category under Honey, so its honey syrup recipe takes the tallow
  without any help from this port. A run without this file confirmed it (docs/runs, 2026-10-09): the recipe
  accepted the tallow either way.

  What it does NOT do for this port is the category icon. It points iconPath at
  Things/Pawn/Animal/Megabee/oldmegabee_east, a texture the ORIGINAL Megabees ships and this port does not, so
  every game start with both mods logs "Could not load Texture2D ... oldmegabee_east" and the category shows the
  red error square. This patch repoints that one path at megabee_east, which this port ships.

  The guard is PatchOperationFindMod on the DISPLAYED NAME of that mod (FindMod reads names, not packageIds) and,
  inside it, PatchOperationConditional on the category def: with that mod absent nothing is touched, and if an
  update of it drops the category the patch does nothing instead of logging a failure. It is NOT MayRequire on an
  <Operation>: nothing reads it there.

  ORDER MATTERS: the category is added by that mod's own patch, so this one has to run after it. About.xml
  declares <loadAfter>TSP.zal.patchhoney2</loadAfter>.
-->
<Patch>

	<Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
		<mods>
			<li>TurtleShroom Productions Proudly Presents: Make Honey EVEN MORE Compatible</li>
		</mods>
		<match Class="PatchOperationConditional">
			<xpath>/Defs/ThingCategoryDef[defName="TSP_ZOURA_MegaBee_Honey_Category"]/iconPath</xpath>
			<match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
				<xpath>/Defs/ThingCategoryDef[defName="TSP_ZOURA_MegaBee_Honey_Category"]/iconPath</xpath>
				<value>
					<iconPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/Megabee/megabee_east</iconPath>
				</value>
			</match>
		</match>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
